WEBVTT

00:00:01.380 --> 00:00:04.980
Satoshi, who aims to battle
the Supreme Monarch, Dande...

00:00:05.350 --> 00:00:10.110
And Go, who dreams of catching every Pokémon
to work his way up to Mew...

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:15.350
This is the story of their lives and adventures.

00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:27.290
The sun shines bright.

00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:29.500
It’s a peaceful day off.

00:00:31.040 --> 00:00:32.550
Sheesh!

00:00:42.280 --> 00:00:43.120
There!

00:00:50.540 --> 00:00:52.760
Mom, this illustration’s yours, isn’t it?

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:56.700
Correct! You really are my daughter.

00:00:56.700 --> 00:00:58.780
Isn’t this me?

00:01:00.010 --> 00:01:04.230
You know I don’t like my bedhair!
Why would you put it in an illustration?!

00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:07.190
Oh, no, that’s just a character!
A completely fictional creation.

00:01:07.190 --> 00:01:09.410
It doesn’t look like you at all.

00:01:09.410 --> 00:01:10.040
Lemme see.

00:01:11.140 --> 00:01:12.420
It’s Sis!

00:01:12.420 --> 00:01:13.980
See?!

00:01:13.980 --> 00:01:16.480
Oh, Sota...

00:01:17.290 --> 00:01:20.080
Oh, dear, it seems
Wanpachi is calling.

00:01:20.080 --> 00:01:22.020
What is it, Wanpachi?

00:01:30.230 --> 00:01:32.940
W-What?
What’s that in your mouth?!

00:01:33.370 --> 00:01:35.830
W-Wait a second, Wanpachi!

00:01:37.320 --> 00:01:38.910
Wanpachi, come here.

00:01:38.910 --> 00:01:40.160
There, there...

00:01:41.610 --> 00:01:42.870
It’s a Mamepato.

00:01:44.020 --> 00:01:44.850
But...

00:01:44.850 --> 00:01:46.070
It’s not moving.

00:01:48.750 --> 00:01:49.990
It’s fine.

00:01:49.990 --> 00:01:51.900
It’s just unconscious.

00:01:53.140 --> 00:01:54.710
What a relief.

00:01:55.420 --> 00:01:58.440
Oh, yeah...
Something hit my window earlier.

00:01:58.440 --> 00:02:00.740
It must have been
this Mamepato.

00:02:10.380 --> 00:02:12.190
It’s injured.

00:02:13.870 --> 00:02:18.160
Let’s look after it
until it can fly again.

00:02:19.030 --> 00:02:20.730
Let me hold it, too!

00:02:20.730 --> 00:02:22.070
Treating its wounds comes first.

00:02:22.070 --> 00:02:22.620
Yeah.

00:02:30.330 --> 00:02:36.960
PocketMonsters

00:02:36.960 --> 00:02:39.380
Hey, you still not ready? C'mon, hurry up!

00:02:39.380 --> 00:02:41.960
You all packed and ready to leave?

00:02:41.960 --> 00:02:44.680
I'll show you this wide mysterious world

00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:47.550
And skip the slow send-off

00:02:47.550 --> 00:02:49.890
Be it through fire or through water

00:02:49.890 --> 00:02:52.560
I'm fumbling blindly through the days

00:02:52.560 --> 00:02:57.060
When I don't even know what the next second will bring

00:02:57.730 --> 00:03:02.320
Each and every one of my memories

00:03:02.320 --> 00:03:06.910
Can always be found inside a Ball

00:03:08.070 --> 00:03:10.830
On 1, 2, 3, dive in!

00:03:10.830 --> 00:03:16.580
I've got the future plans I imagined in my pocket

00:03:18.540 --> 00:03:23.590
Greeting someone new is always fresh

00:03:23.590 --> 00:03:27.800
No need (No need!) to hesitate! Try! (Try!)

00:03:27.800 --> 00:03:29.140
Let's have a fight!

00:03:29.140 --> 00:03:31.850
1: Once the battle's done

00:03:31.850 --> 00:03:33.680
2: And we're laughing or crying

00:03:33.680 --> 00:03:38.020
On 3, let's be friends!

00:03:39.310 --> 00:03:44.690
Any day and every day, that's always been my rule

00:03:44.690 --> 00:03:50.030
With this unpredictable, boundless world awaiting

00:03:50.030 --> 00:03:52.530
Let's go! Every time you trip and fall

00:03:52.530 --> 00:03:56.660
Let's go! You pick yourself up by my side

00:03:56.660 --> 00:03:58.460
I choose you!

00:04:02.040 --> 00:04:07.470
Wanpachi's Feelings
A Jealous Fit!

00:04:08.100 --> 00:04:09.850
This is Sakuragi Park.

00:04:09.850 --> 00:04:13.850
As usual, Satoshi is getting in
some early morning training.

00:04:21.070 --> 00:04:22.400
Block it with Force Palm!

00:04:31.500 --> 00:04:33.220
Good going, both of you!

00:04:33.220 --> 00:04:33.660
Now, next is—

00:04:33.660 --> 00:04:34.650
Satoshi!
Now, next is—

00:04:34.650 --> 00:04:36.000
Satoshi!

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:38.040
Have you seen Messon?

00:04:38.040 --> 00:04:39.820
What? No.

00:04:39.820 --> 00:04:41.340
I can’t find it.

00:04:41.340 --> 00:04:44.490
Again? Sure it’s not
just camouflaged?

00:04:44.490 --> 00:04:47.630
I thought it might be,
so I looked around, but...

00:04:51.020 --> 00:04:51.960
Found you!

00:04:51.960 --> 00:04:52.940
Come on!

00:04:58.330 --> 00:05:00.820
Oh, it was just Barrierd?

00:05:01.880 --> 00:05:03.650
I couldn’t find it anywhere.

00:05:05.650 --> 00:05:07.660
All right!
Let’s help look for Messon!

00:05:11.570 --> 00:05:12.040
Go!

00:05:12.040 --> 00:05:13.290
Yeah.

00:05:26.600 --> 00:05:27.930
This means...

00:05:27.930 --> 00:05:29.380
Messon is...

00:05:29.380 --> 00:05:31.680
...definitely here...!

00:05:34.590 --> 00:05:38.420
Messon!
Messon, where are you?

00:05:38.420 --> 00:05:39.650
I know!

00:05:40.480 --> 00:05:45.070
Butterfree! Morphon!
Stun Spore!

00:05:54.410 --> 00:05:55.040
There!

00:05:59.420 --> 00:06:01.840
Kairyu!
Do your thing with Messon!

00:06:16.240 --> 00:06:17.660
What an appetite.

00:06:17.660 --> 00:06:18.850
Yeah.

00:06:21.300 --> 00:06:23.600
I guess it said
thanks for the food?

00:06:23.600 --> 00:06:25.690
Mamepato, I’m Sota.

00:06:25.690 --> 00:06:28.910
This is my sister Koharu,
and these are my mom and dad.

00:06:36.120 --> 00:06:38.510
Mamepato, this is Wanpachi.

00:06:42.460 --> 00:06:44.470
Hey, wait!

00:06:46.010 --> 00:06:47.510
Oh, dear...

00:06:48.040 --> 00:06:49.590
Wait! Wait!

00:06:54.100 --> 00:06:56.470
Wanpachi, don’t chase after it.

00:07:24.850 --> 00:07:26.250
What’s going on?

00:07:26.250 --> 00:07:29.460
Looks like Mamepato
likes Wanpachi’s back.

00:07:29.460 --> 00:07:32.810
But it was so scared of him
just a second ago.

00:07:32.810 --> 00:07:35.560
It’s forgotten that it was scared.

00:07:35.560 --> 00:07:36.640
<i>What?</i>

00:07:37.060 --> 00:07:40.890
Mamepato follows its trainer’s orders
as best it can,

00:07:41.280 --> 00:07:44.180
but they sometimes fail to understand
complicated commands.

00:07:44.180 --> 00:07:45.730
It’s very forgetful,

00:07:45.730 --> 00:07:49.140
and sometimes forgets that
it even <i>received</i> an order.

00:07:49.140 --> 00:07:50.920
Really? That’s so cute!

00:07:50.920 --> 00:07:52.440
Super cute!

00:07:52.440 --> 00:07:55.650
Cute... Really?

00:07:58.050 --> 00:07:59.640
I guess it is!

00:08:00.410 --> 00:08:02.250
It’s nice to meet you,
Mamepato!

00:08:02.250 --> 00:08:05.190
Make yourself at home.

00:08:05.190 --> 00:08:06.290
Wanpachi?

00:08:25.810 --> 00:08:27.640
Welcome in, Mamepato.

00:08:35.430 --> 00:08:36.680
You want to see?

00:08:45.130 --> 00:08:49.010
Quite a few girls in my class
read this magazine...

00:08:49.770 --> 00:08:51.700
You like frizzy hair?

00:08:54.520 --> 00:08:55.930
I guess you do.

00:09:17.430 --> 00:09:19.060
Isn’t it beautiful?

00:09:45.220 --> 00:09:47.100
Isn’t Mamepato cute?

00:09:47.560 --> 00:09:49.290
Eat up.

00:09:51.130 --> 00:09:54.740
Mamepato seems to be
doing better than yesterday.

00:09:58.760 --> 00:10:01.140
Hey, Wanpachi, stop that!

00:10:01.660 --> 00:10:03.950
You’ll tear my uniform!

00:10:03.950 --> 00:10:05.410
Wanpachi?

00:10:05.410 --> 00:10:07.110
What could be wrong?

00:10:09.460 --> 00:10:11.250
It must be jealousy.

00:10:11.700 --> 00:10:12.880
Jealousy?

00:10:12.880 --> 00:10:16.440
Wanpachi is like our youngest child.

00:10:16.440 --> 00:10:18.930
Everyone in the family loves him.

00:10:18.930 --> 00:10:20.220
I suppose.

00:10:20.220 --> 00:10:24.090
But now Mamepato has
taken that “youngest child” spot,

00:10:24.090 --> 00:10:27.140
and even his precious Koharu
is fixated on Mamepato.

00:10:27.140 --> 00:10:28.840
I see.

00:10:28.840 --> 00:10:30.600
I don’t get it.

00:10:30.600 --> 00:10:33.480
Dad, it’s time for us to go!

00:10:33.480 --> 00:10:35.100
Oh, of course!

00:10:35.100 --> 00:10:39.990
I’ll look into whether there are any reports
of a missing Mamepato.

00:10:39.990 --> 00:10:41.990
Please do.

00:10:42.540 --> 00:10:44.120
See you later!

00:10:52.850 --> 00:10:54.880
It really has
taken a shine to them.

00:10:56.770 --> 00:10:58.630
See you after school!

00:11:01.740 --> 00:11:03.470
You’re doing great, Wanpachi.

00:11:03.470 --> 00:11:05.260
It’s like you’re
Mamepato’s big brother.

00:11:17.700 --> 00:11:19.030
That ought to do it.

00:11:19.030 --> 00:11:22.030
That ought to do what,
Director?

00:11:22.740 --> 00:11:25.930
We took in an injured
Mamepato yesterday.

00:11:25.930 --> 00:11:27.880
Seems like it crashed into our window.

00:11:28.470 --> 00:11:31.340
I just reported it on
social networking sites.

00:11:31.340 --> 00:11:33.540
It might be a lost Pokémon.

00:11:33.540 --> 00:11:34.880
I see.

00:11:34.880 --> 00:11:36.680
I’ve had that happen, too.

00:11:36.680 --> 00:11:38.180
Something crashing into my window.

00:11:38.180 --> 00:11:42.750
If the glass is really clear,
bird Pokémon don’t always notice it.

00:11:42.750 --> 00:11:45.110
Thankfully, it didn’t get hurt
that bad in my case.

00:11:45.110 --> 00:11:47.560
It flew off again right away.

00:11:50.440 --> 00:11:52.140
What’cha gonna do after school?

00:11:52.140 --> 00:11:55.060
Let’s go to the bay
to look for Pokémon!

00:11:55.060 --> 00:11:56.600
Great idea!

00:11:59.350 --> 00:12:05.060
I’m sure Mamepato
is dying to fly like that again.

00:12:05.060 --> 00:12:10.040
Let’s look after it
until it can fly again.

00:12:10.510 --> 00:12:13.460
Until it can fly again, huh?

00:12:14.750 --> 00:12:15.450
PocketMonsters

00:12:15.450 --> 00:12:17.050
Pocket Monsters!
PocketMonsters

00:12:17.050 --> 00:12:21.550
PocketMonsters

00:12:21.550 --> 00:12:26.470
Flying
. Normal .
Mamepato
PocketMonsters

00:12:28.610 --> 00:12:30.150
See you tomorrow.

00:12:39.920 --> 00:12:42.320
Wanpachi, Mamepato, I’m back.

00:12:54.690 --> 00:12:55.710
What’s wrong, Wanpachi?

00:12:57.380 --> 00:12:59.850
Oh, Koharu?

00:13:00.920 --> 00:13:04.030
Is this the Mamepato
the Director mentioned?

00:13:08.050 --> 00:13:09.580
Wanpachi?

00:13:13.090 --> 00:13:14.260
What’s going on?

00:13:14.870 --> 00:13:16.310
It’s jealousy.

00:13:16.310 --> 00:13:17.230
Jealousy?

00:13:17.230 --> 00:13:21.610
Wanpachi is annoyed at Mamepato
for hogging Koharu’s attention.

00:13:21.610 --> 00:13:22.860
Really?

00:13:23.320 --> 00:13:28.190
I’m treating them both
the same way, though...

00:13:30.280 --> 00:13:34.040
So all he wants is for Mamepato
to stop clinging to Koharu.

00:13:34.040 --> 00:13:35.130
So it seems.

00:13:35.760 --> 00:13:37.830
This jealousy thing
is pretty bothersome.

00:13:38.260 --> 00:13:40.140
Oh, don’t say that.

00:13:40.140 --> 00:13:44.930
Wanpachi’s acting pretty tame
compared to how you were back in the day.

00:13:48.300 --> 00:13:51.240
I remember what
she was like back then!

00:13:51.240 --> 00:13:52.230
What?

00:13:52.230 --> 00:13:55.800
Back when I was still a student
at the Director’s laboratory...

00:13:55.800 --> 00:13:59.700
A friend from the Galar Region
sent me Wanpachi.

00:13:59.700 --> 00:14:03.170
This was before Sota was born,
back when you were still an only child.

00:14:03.170 --> 00:14:05.670
You got really jealous of Wanpachi.

00:14:05.670 --> 00:14:06.820
I did?

00:14:06.820 --> 00:14:10.230
Back then, it seemed like
you were thinking,

00:14:10.230 --> 00:14:13.910
“Wanpachi’s gonna steal
Mom and Dad from me!”

00:14:13.950 --> 00:14:17.620
Mister Renji!
Stop petting Wanpachi!

00:14:18.190 --> 00:14:19.670
You were even yelling at me.

00:14:19.670 --> 00:14:23.250
I said that?!
I don’t remember at all!

00:14:23.250 --> 00:14:26.900
But Galar Pokémon are a rare sight,

00:14:26.900 --> 00:14:31.100
so I sneakily studied Wanpachi
when you weren’t looking.

00:14:31.550 --> 00:14:37.180
Your mom and I were careful not to be too affectionate
to Wanpachi when you were around, too.

00:14:38.280 --> 00:14:41.270
That’s really embarrassing...
I was way too childish!

00:14:43.020 --> 00:14:46.720
It’s perfectly normal.
Nothing to be ashamed of.

00:14:46.720 --> 00:14:48.830
Speaking from experience,
Kikuna?

00:14:48.830 --> 00:14:53.030
It was my little sister
I was jealous of, but yes.

00:14:53.460 --> 00:14:57.080
So, how did Koharu and
Wanpachi become friends?

00:14:57.800 --> 00:15:00.920
One day, Koharu told Wanpachi...

00:15:00.920 --> 00:15:03.810
...that she wished he’d just go away.

00:15:03.810 --> 00:15:06.370
What?!
Past me was awful!

00:15:06.370 --> 00:15:08.870
And then the “incident” occurred.

00:15:08.870 --> 00:15:09.800
Incident?

00:15:09.800 --> 00:15:11.800
The Runaway Wanpachi Incident.

00:15:12.170 --> 00:15:13.300
Runaway...?

00:15:13.350 --> 00:15:16.870
I wish you’d just go away!

00:15:25.970 --> 00:15:27.870
What could have happened?

00:15:27.870 --> 00:15:29.960
Where could he have gone?

00:15:33.070 --> 00:15:34.550
What’s wrong?

00:15:34.550 --> 00:15:36.610
Wanpachi has disappeared.

00:15:36.610 --> 00:15:37.650
Disappeared?

00:15:37.650 --> 00:15:39.030
Don’t worry.

00:15:39.030 --> 00:15:41.060
Your Dad will find him!

00:15:42.240 --> 00:15:44.680
Just go back to bed.

00:15:49.940 --> 00:15:51.860
Look, this is Wanpachi!

00:16:04.290 --> 00:16:05.960
Don’t follow me.

00:16:08.320 --> 00:16:09.310
No!

00:16:19.950 --> 00:16:25.260
Wanpachi...

00:16:26.180 --> 00:16:27.210
Where are you?

00:16:36.070 --> 00:16:38.810
Where... Where did you go?

00:16:54.780 --> 00:16:58.000
I went looking for Wanpachi,

00:16:58.850 --> 00:17:00.730
then some Konpang
frightened me...

00:17:02.120 --> 00:17:03.370
You remember?

00:17:04.510 --> 00:17:05.870
Then Wanpachi came and...

00:17:20.070 --> 00:17:21.770
That tickles, Wanpachi!

00:17:22.240 --> 00:17:23.640
I told you it tickles!

00:17:24.940 --> 00:17:26.590
Ever since then,

00:17:26.590 --> 00:17:29.310
Wanpachi has only slept
in Koharu’s room,

00:17:29.310 --> 00:17:32.610
and will only eat the Pokémon Food
Koharu puts out for him.

00:17:33.590 --> 00:17:36.290
Wanpachi must have been happy...

00:17:36.290 --> 00:17:39.250
...that Koharu went to look for him.

00:17:44.450 --> 00:17:45.160
Wanpachi?!

00:18:06.570 --> 00:18:07.940
Wanpachi! Mamepato!

00:18:09.300 --> 00:18:10.440
Onidrill?!

00:18:21.510 --> 00:18:22.770
Wanpachi...

00:18:22.770 --> 00:18:24.650
Director, we have to do something!

00:18:24.650 --> 00:18:27.280
Leave it to Koharu and Wanpachi.

00:18:32.370 --> 00:18:34.190
Koharu! Wanpachi!

00:18:34.190 --> 00:18:37.190
His jealousy shows how close he is to you.

00:18:37.190 --> 00:18:39.330
Together, you can definitely
fight that thing.

00:18:39.330 --> 00:18:40.300
Dad...

00:18:40.300 --> 00:18:41.800
Hang in there, Koharu!

00:18:43.680 --> 00:18:44.810
You got this!

00:18:48.060 --> 00:18:51.060
All right!
Let’s go, Wanpachi!

00:18:53.980 --> 00:18:55.330
Spark!

00:19:06.410 --> 00:19:07.540
You did it!

00:19:07.540 --> 00:19:08.540
You took it down!

00:19:26.860 --> 00:19:28.390
Onidrill!

00:19:28.390 --> 00:19:31.520
W-Wait! I wanna catch you!

00:19:39.550 --> 00:19:43.230
You’ve taken such good care
of my Mamepato!

00:19:43.230 --> 00:19:46.030
I really don’t know how
I could ever thank you!

00:19:50.450 --> 00:19:54.500
This one is the leader
of my Mamepato Race team.

00:19:54.500 --> 00:19:55.840
<i>Leader?</i>

00:19:56.350 --> 00:19:57.680
It’s super quick,

00:19:57.680 --> 00:20:01.190
and cares more than anyone
for its teammates.

00:20:01.190 --> 00:20:03.840
Its leadership skills
are unmatched.

00:20:04.230 --> 00:20:06.000
I see.

00:20:06.000 --> 00:20:08.380
Mamepato’s leaving?

00:20:08.380 --> 00:20:12.230
That’s right, Sota.
Mamepato’s going back to its real home.

00:20:13.020 --> 00:20:15.360
Thank you for looking after it!

00:20:15.790 --> 00:20:18.860
But we just became friends...

00:20:18.860 --> 00:20:20.010
Sota.

00:20:20.010 --> 00:20:21.860
Look at Mamepato.

00:20:22.720 --> 00:20:26.870
It loves its real trainer a lot.

00:20:28.780 --> 00:20:29.980
I guess you’re right.

00:20:37.230 --> 00:20:39.870
Mamepato!
Come visit again sometime!

00:20:39.870 --> 00:20:41.630
We’re waiting for you!

00:20:49.510 --> 00:20:52.980
It sure is quiet here
without Mamepato.

00:20:52.980 --> 00:20:54.570
Even though it was only here...

00:20:54.570 --> 00:20:57.270
...for two days!

00:20:57.850 --> 00:21:00.140
Did Dad write this book?

00:21:00.140 --> 00:21:01.350
That’s right.

00:21:01.350 --> 00:21:03.430
Looks complicated.

00:21:03.430 --> 00:21:05.230
This book...

00:21:05.640 --> 00:21:10.750
...is all about what
we should do in the world...

00:21:10.750 --> 00:21:15.210
...to make sure people and Pokémon
can keep living together in peace.

00:21:15.210 --> 00:21:20.590
How to make sure people and Pokémon
can keep living together in peace, huh?

00:21:21.680 --> 00:21:23.440
Koharu! Wanpachi!

00:21:23.440 --> 00:21:26.480
His jealousy shows how close he is to you.

00:21:26.480 --> 00:21:28.680
Together, you can definitely
fight that thing.

00:21:29.560 --> 00:21:31.810
I guess Dad’s pretty cool.

00:21:31.810 --> 00:21:34.610
That’s right, he is.

00:21:34.610 --> 00:21:35.890
Didn’t you know?

00:21:36.630 --> 00:21:39.580
Through meeting and
saying goodbye to Mamepato,

00:21:39.580 --> 00:21:43.310
Koharu has gotten just a little bit
closer to the Pokémon.

00:21:45.990 --> 00:21:47.280
Let’s play Pokémon Shiritori!

00:21:47.280 --> 00:21:49.990
(Mew → Zamazenta Ver.)

00:21:49.990 --> 00:21:50.280
